# AUTOPILOT DONE — Customer Zero Email P0 closure

## 1. ROSA PRE-FLIGHT
Read: rosa.yaml, docs/architecture.md, existing Gmail OAuth (google-tokens,
oauth-state, gmail-adapter), credential layer (credential-resolver,
google_oauth_tokens), command-center routing, conversation durability,
approval system, marketing work. No runtime/credential/OAuth redesign.
Gmail OAuth untouched. No Calendar/Drive. No new department.

## 2. EXISTING EMAIL ARCHITECTURE FOUND
Capability vocabulary already provider-independent (email.read/search/draft/
send.personal), GmailAdapter (read/search/draft/send), durable Google token
store, email-delivery-adapter (Resend, campaigns). MISSING: email send routing
in chat, multi-turn pending email state, corporate (non-Google) provider.

## 3. RED-ERROR LAST_SUCCESSFUL_CHECKPOINT
POST /conversations/{id}/messages 200 (22:52:43, 8.5s) — the CEO's email
request was understood and Elvira asked for missing info.

## 4. RED-ERROR FIRST_FAILED_CHECKPOINT
The follow-up POST /conversations/{id}/messages → **HTTP 499 after 28s**
(Railway log 22:53:33) — the client closed the request while the engine
(OpenClaw, 120s timeout) was still processing the generic `delegate_marketing`
turn. Portal `postJson` returned null → ChatRoute rendered
"Departify no ha podido responderte ahora mismo."

## 5. ROOT CAUSE
Email requests fell into `delegate_marketing` → engine/LLM turn (slow,
unbounded for UX, no email context) and there was NO pending-email state, so a
follow-up could not continue the objective. The 28s+ engine turn exceeded the
client's patience → 499 → red error, work lost.

## 6. FILES CHANGED
pending-email.ts (new), email-capability.ts (new), corporate-email-store.ts (new),
corporate-email-adapter.ts (new), command-center.ts, customer-zero-session.ts,
customer-zero-v2.ts, main.ts, portal api.ts / ConnectionsRoute.tsx / tokens.css,
package.json + pnpm-lock (imapflow, nodemailer), migration
20260811090000_email_accounts.sql, tests customer-zero-06/07 + portal tests.

## 7. EMAIL CAPABILITY ARCHITECTURE
email.read/search/compose/send boundary; provider resolution:
corporate (IMAP/SMTP) first, Google fallback. Business code never names a
provider. Gmail is a provider, not the capability.

## 8. GMAIL PROVIDER BEHAVIOR
Unchanged OAuth; reads via presenter (no query jargon); sends via
GmailAdapter.sendMessage through the capability boundary; durable send evidence
(messageId, recipient, sentAt).

## 9. IMAP PROVIDER BEHAVIOR
imapflow, bounded 15s; read inbox (unseen→recent), presents via the same
business presenter. Valid creds → operational (probe IMAP connect + INBOX).

## 10. SMTP PROVIDER BEHAVIOR
nodemailer, bounded; send via transporter.sendMail; probe = verify() session
(never sends mail). Operational only when IMAP AND SMTP probes succeed.

## 11. CREDENTIAL SECURITY
Corporate password stored server-side (email_accounts, service-role only, RLS
block-all, org+user scoped), NEVER returned by APIs, never logged, never in
chat/DNA/model. Same posture as Google tokens.

## 12. CONNECTION STATE MODEL
Connected = durable credentials + real bounded probe success
(operationalVerifiedAt). Probe failure → honest non-connected state with a
business reason. No "connected" without capability.

## 13. MULTI-TURN CONTINUATION FIX
pendingEmailWork (session): recipient/objective/missingFields/draft/status.
Follow-ups absorb missing info, preserve recipient+objective, rebuild draft,
never fall to generic routing, never pick Mautic, never emit the red error.
Deterministic pipeline — no engine dependency.

## 14. APPROVAL FLOW
Conversational: draft shown with "¿Lo envío? Responde «sí, envíalo»"; approval
sends; cancellation cancels; new info rebuilds the draft.

## 15. SEND-RESULT DURABILITY
PendingEmailWork.sendResult { provider, recipient, sentAt, providerMessageId }
persisted on the session + the send confirmation is a durable conversation
message. Failed sends never report success; draft survives for retry.

## 16. PROMPT-INJECTION BOUNDARY
Email body is DATA: malicious content is echoed as draft content to send,
never executed as instructions (CZ06 Z test).

## 17. ORG ISOLATION
Credential stores + capability resolution are org-scoped; cross-org access
rejected (CZ06 X, CZ07 X tests).

## 18. UX CHANGES
/conexiones → "Correo" capability with providers: Google/Gmail (Conectar),
Microsoft 365 (honest "Próximamente"), Otro correo de empresa (IMAP/SMTP form).
Product wording everywhere; contextual "Conecta tu correo" card when email is
needed but not connected.

## 19. TESTS ADDED
CZ06 (10): multi-turn draft/approval/send, missing-info continuation,
"Conecta tu correo", no unnecessary card, no Mautic/red error, failed send,
org isolation, prompt-injection. CZ07 (6): corporate probe ok/invalid,
no credential leakage, corporate send/read dispatch, org isolation.

